        ("Signs of shock include:",
         ["Warm, dry, pink skin and calm breathing", "Pale, cool, clammy skin, rapid pulse, and confusion or anxiety", "A slow pulse and deep sleep", "Itchy skin only"], 1),
        ("The first treatment for life-threatening bleeding is:",
         ["A bandage, loosely applied", "Firm, direct pressure with a dressing", "Elevation only", "Washing the wound thoroughly first"], 1),
        ("A dressing becomes soaked with blood. You should:",
         ["Remove it and apply a fresh one", "Add more dressings on top and keep pressing", "Stop pressing to let it air out", "Apply a tourniquet to every wound"], 1),
        ("For a fresh burn, the correct first aid is:",
         ["Ice directly on the burn", "Butter or ointment right away", "Cool running water for at least 10 minutes, then cover loosely", "Pop all blisters"], 2),
